1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:06,710
Our robot now knows which cup to grasp, but its next movement still needs a representation.
机器人现在知道要抓哪个杯子，但下一步动作仍然需要一种表示。

2
00:00:07,690 --> 00:00:13,590
Three different decisions are often mixed together: action meaning, temporal grouping, and prediction method.
三个不同决定经常被混在一起：动作含义、时间分组，以及预测方法。

3
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:19,310
Meaning specifies joint targets or Cartesian changes, with units and coordinate conventions.
动作含义规定关节目标或笛卡尔变化，以及单位和坐标约定。

4
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:24,390
Grouping specifies whether the model predicts one command or several commands together.
时间分组规定模型预测一条指令，还是一起预测多条指令。

5
00:00:24,950 --> 00:00:30,775
Prediction specifies tokens, regression, diffusion, or a learned flow over continuous actions.
预测方法则选择 token、回归、扩散，或者连续动作上的学习流。

6
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:35,290
Changing one decision does not logically require changing the other two.
改变其中一个决定，并不意味着必须同时改变另外两个。

7
00:00:35,839 --> 00:00:41,519
A physical displacement is continuous even when a model represents it with a discrete token.
物理位移是连续量，即使模型用离散 token 来表示它。

8
00:00:42,019 --> 00:00:47,659
A tokenizer assigns that displacement to a code, and a decoder maps the code back to a number.
分词器把位移分配给一个编码，解码器再把编码还原成数值。

9
00:00:48,059 --> 00:00:53,559
Therefore, token prediction does not imply that the robot can occupy only a few physical positions.
因此，预测 token 不代表机器人只能停在少数几个物理位置。

10
00:00:54,059 --> 00:00:58,979
The controller executes decoded references and may interpolate between them over time.
控制器执行解码后的参考，还可能在时间上对这些参考进行插值。

11
00:00:59,419 --> 00:01:05,124
Quantization does introduce approximation error, and its consequences depend on the task's tolerance.
但量化确实会引入近似误差，其影响取决于任务容差。

12
00:01:05,139 --> 00:01:10,859
A coarse movement representation may suffice for approaching a cup but struggle near a tight insertion.
接近杯子时够用的粗糙动作表示，在紧配合插入附近可能就不够了。

13
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:16,787
Consider an illustrative translation range from minus four to plus four centimeters.
考虑一个教学平移范围：从负四厘米到正四厘米。

14
00:01:17,607 --> 00:01:21,067
Divide it into eight equal bins and decode each bin to its center.
把这个范围分成八个等宽分箱，每个分箱解码成中心值。

15
00:01:21,507 --> 00:01:26,787
Each bin is one centimeter wide, giving a maximum half-centimeter error inside the range.
每个分箱宽一厘米，因此范围内最大误差是半厘米。

16
00:01:27,207 --> 00:01:32,567
A requested one point two centimeters becomes one point five, an error of three millimeters.
要求移动一点二厘米，会变成一点五厘米，误差为三毫米。

17
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:38,392
Increasing the bin count reduces this bound, but changes prediction difficulty and sequence design.
增加分箱数量能够降低这个误差上界，但也会改变预测难度和序列设计。

18
00:01:38,407 --> 00:01:42,825
Clipping an out-of-range command creates additional error beyond this simple bound.
把范围外指令裁剪回范围内，还会产生超出这个简单上界的误差。

19
00:01:43,275 --> 00:01:49,135
An autoregressive decoder predicts the next token using the observation and previous tokens.
自回归解码器根据观测和之前的 token，预测下一个 token。

20
00:01:49,915 --> 00:01:54,775
Training commonly minimizes negative log probability of the demonstrated token sequence.
训练通常最小化示范 token 序列的负对数概率。

21
00:01:55,235 --> 00:02:00,595
The product of conditional probabilities defines the probability assigned to the entire sequence.
各条件概率的乘积，定义了整段序列获得的概率。

22
00:02:01,135 --> 00:02:07,020
This is convenient for language-model backbones, but serial generation creates a dependency chain.
这种方式适合语言模型主干，但串行生成会形成一条依赖链。

23
00:02:07,035 --> 00:02:13,235
If a chunk contains many dimensions and timesteps, naive binning can produce a long sequence.
如果一个动作块包含很多维度和时间步，朴素分箱就可能产生很长的序列。

24
00:02:14,015 --> 00:02:17,635
Token count is thus a systems issue as well as a representational choice.
所以 token 数量既是表示选择，也是系统工程问题。

25
00:02:18,283 --> 00:02:24,323
FAST addresses the redundancy of representing every action dimension at every timestep separately.
FAST 处理的是：每一时刻、每个动作维度分别编码所产生的冗余。

26
00:02:24,883 --> 00:02:29,763
Follow its original figure from left to right, starting with a normalized action chunk.
沿着原图从左向右看，首先输入的是归一化动作块。

27
00:02:30,243 --> 00:02:36,363
A discrete cosine transform expresses each action channel using frequency components across time.
离散余弦变换，把各动作通道表示成沿时间变化的频率分量。

28
00:02:36,863 --> 00:02:42,063
The coefficients are quantized and serialized, then compressed further with byte-pair encoding.
这些系数随后被量化、序列化，再通过字节对编码进一步压缩。

29
00:02:42,823 --> 00:02:46,648
Decoding reverses the process to recover a continuous action sequence.
解码时逆转这个过程，还原连续动作序列。

30
00:02:46,663 --> 00:02:52,503
Smooth, correlated motion can therefore use a different code length than arbitrary independent samples.
因此，平滑且相关的动作，与任意独立采样的动作，可以具有不同的编码长度。

31
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:59,551
A tokenizer can reconstruct recorded motions accurately while the policy predicts its codes poorly.
分词器可能准确还原已记录动作，但策略仍然难以预测正确编码。

32
00:03:00,151 --> 00:03:05,251
Reconstruction tests the representation; rollout tests the behavior of the learned policy.
这是不同的测量：重建检验表示，实际运行检验学习到的控制策略。

33
00:03:05,931 --> 00:03:10,211
FAST is an action tokenizer, not a complete robot policy by itself.
FAST 是动作分词器，本身不是一个完整的机器人策略。

34
00:03:10,611 --> 00:03:17,071
A model using FAST still needs observations, task conditioning, training data, and an execution schedule.
使用 FAST 的模型，仍然需要观测、任务条件、训练数据，以及执行时序。

35
00:03:17,851 --> 00:03:22,951
Likewise, faster training does not prove lower end-to-end response latency on a particular robot.
同样，训练更快，并不能证明某台机器人上的端到端反应延迟更低。

36
00:03:23,491 --> 00:03:28,991
Always follow the reported quantity: compression, training time, action throughput, or task completion.
必须看清实际报告的量：压缩率、训练时间、动作吞吐，还是任务完成表现。

37
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:34,360
Action chunking groups several future commands into a single prediction problem.
动作分块把多条未来指令，组合成一个预测问题。

38
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:40,680
It can reduce repeated decisions and help represent coherent motions, including pauses in demonstrations.
它可以减少重复决策，也有助于表示连贯动作，包括示范中的停顿。

39
00:03:41,340 --> 00:03:47,100
ACT uses a Transformer and a conditional variational autoencoder during training to model action chunks.
ACT 用 Transformer，并在训练中采用条件变分自编码器，来建模动作块。

40
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:52,660
Its temporal ensembling combines overlapping predictions referring to the same future timestep.
它的时间集成，会合并指向同一未来时间步的重叠预测。

41
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:56,845
This is distinct from taking the average of all future steps in one chunk.
这与把一个动作块内所有未来时间步直接平均，并不是一回事。

42
00:03:56,860 --> 00:04:02,800
And chunking is compatible with discrete tokens, continuous regression, diffusion, or flow matching.
同时，动作分块可以搭配离散 token、连续回归、扩散，或者流匹配。

43
00:04:03,446 --> 00:04:10,386
A continuous regression head predicts numerical actions directly, often producing a full chunk in parallel.
连续回归头直接预测数值动作，通常可以并行输出完整动作块。

44
00:04:10,866 --> 00:04:16,046
An L1 objective penalizes absolute coordinate differences from demonstrated actions.
L1 目标惩罚预测动作与示范动作在各坐标上的绝对差值。

45
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:22,446
An L2 objective instead penalizes squared differences, which weights larger errors more strongly.
L2 目标则惩罚平方差，因此对较大误差施加更大权重。

46
00:04:22,986 --> 00:04:28,831
OpenVLA-OFT shows why this simple family belongs in a serious comparison of fine-tuning recipes.
OpenVLA-OFT 说明，在认真比较微调方案时，这类简单方法不能缺席。

47
00:04:28,846 --> 00:04:35,346
Its recipe combines parallel decoding, action chunks, continuous outputs, and L1 regression.
其方案结合了并行解码、动作分块、连续输出，以及 L1 回归。

48
00:04:35,866 --> 00:04:41,966
The result is a concrete configuration, not proof that regression universally beats every generative decoder.
这个结果对应具体配置，并不证明回归在所有情况下都胜过生成式解码器。

49
00:04:42,503 --> 00:04:47,243
Imagine that the gripper can reach the cup by moving left or right around an obstacle.
想象夹爪可以从障碍左侧，或者右侧，绕过去拿杯子。

50
00:04:47,783 --> 00:04:52,863
Both demonstrated routes succeed, but their pointwise mean may pass straight through the obstacle.
两种示范路线都能成功，但逐点平均后的路线可能直接穿过障碍。

51
00:04:53,423 --> 00:04:57,843
This teaching example explains why a multimodal action distribution can matter.
这个教学例子解释了：为什么多峰动作分布有时十分重要。

52
00:04:58,203 --> 00:05:03,803
A deterministic loss may summarize incompatible choices instead of committing to one coherent route.
确定性损失可能把不兼容的选择概括到一起，而不是选定一条连贯路线。

53
00:05:04,503 --> 00:05:10,188
Generative policies can represent alternatives, although successful training and sampling are still required.
生成式策略能够表示不同选择，但仍然需要成功的训练和采样。

54
00:05:10,203 --> 00:05:15,323
Neither stochasticity nor a smooth-looking trajectory is a guarantee against physical collision.
随机性或者看起来平滑的轨迹，都不是避免物理碰撞的保证。

55
00:05:15,971 --> 00:05:21,851
Diffusion Policy begins inference with a noisy action sequence and repeatedly refines it.
Diffusion Policy 在推理时，从一个含噪动作序列开始，反复进行修正。

56
00:05:22,091 --> 00:05:26,651
During training, known noise is added to demonstrations at sampled noise levels.
训练时，会在采样的噪声等级下，给示范动作加入已知噪声。

57
00:05:27,071 --> 00:05:31,431
The network learns a denoising objective while conditioned on the robot's observations.
网络在机器人观测条件下，学习一个去噪目标。

58
00:05:31,911 --> 00:05:37,871
At deployment, a sampling procedure uses this learned information to generate a coherent action chunk.
部署时，采样过程利用这些学习到的信息，生成连贯动作块。

59
00:05:38,231 --> 00:05:43,456
The refinement steps happen inside inference; they are not separate physical actions of the robot.
这些修正步骤发生在模型推理内部，并不是机器人分别执行的物理动作。

60
00:05:43,471 --> 00:05:49,391
Their computational cost must therefore be included when measuring the time before commands become available.
因此，测量指令可用之前的等待时间时，必须把这些计算成本算进去。

61
00:05:50,018 --> 00:05:56,478
For a simple flow-matching construction, interpolate between random noise and a demonstrated action chunk.
在一种简单的流匹配构造中，我们在随机噪声与示范动作块之间插值。

62
00:05:56,818 --> 00:06:02,478
At interpolation time tau, combine noise with weight one minus tau and actions with weight tau.
在插值时刻 tau，噪声权重是一减 tau，动作权重是 tau。

63
00:06:02,738 --> 00:06:07,498
The target velocity along this straight path is the action chunk minus the sampled noise.
沿这条直线路径的目标速度，就是动作块减去采样噪声。

64
00:06:07,938 --> 00:06:12,598
The network learns that velocity conditioned on observations and interpolation time.
网络根据观测和插值时刻，学习这个速度。

65
00:06:12,818 --> 00:06:18,183
At inference, numerical integration transports a noise sample toward the learned action distribution.
推理时，数值积分把噪声样本输运到学习到的动作分布附近。

66
00:06:18,198 --> 00:06:23,258
Tau describes generative computation, not the seconds elapsed in the physical task.
tau 描述的是生成过程中的计算进度，不是物理任务经过的秒数。

67
00:06:23,824 --> 00:06:30,784
Autoregression factors a token sequence; diffusion and flow iteratively generate continuous samples.
自回归分解 token 序列；扩散和流匹配则迭代生成连续样本。

68
00:06:31,464 --> 00:06:36,044
Parallel regression directly predicts continuous coordinates under a supervised loss.
并行回归在监督损失下，直接预测连续坐标。

69
00:06:36,564 --> 00:06:41,564
These descriptions explain mechanisms, but do not establish a universal speed ranking.
这些描述解释了机制，却不能建立一个普遍成立的速度排名。

70
00:06:41,904 --> 00:06:47,649
Actual cost depends on model size, sequence length, sampling steps, caching, precision, and hardware.
实际开销取决于模型规模、序列长度、采样步数、缓存、精度，以及硬件。

71
00:06:47,664 --> 00:06:54,004
Likewise, precision depends on data quality and the control interface, not only decoder vocabulary.
同样，精度取决于数据质量与控制接口，而不只是解码器采用什么术语。

72
00:06:54,784 --> 00:06:59,984
Keep these factors visible when someone attributes every improvement to a single architectural ingredient.
当有人把所有提升归因于一个架构组件时，要把这些因素同时摆出来。

73
00:07:00,751 --> 00:07:05,431
Now move the cup while the robot is executing a previously generated chunk.
现在，在机器人执行上一段动作块时，把杯子挪走。

74
00:07:06,031 --> 00:07:11,311
Newly generated actions cannot simply replace commands that have already run or are committed to run.
新生成动作，不能直接替换已经执行，或者确定即将执行的指令。

75
00:07:11,691 --> 00:07:16,731
If two chunks disagree at their boundary, switching between them can introduce a sudden jump.
如果两个动作块在交界处不一致，切换时就可能产生突然跳变。

76
00:07:17,051 --> 00:07:21,551
Choosing a decoder therefore does not finish the problem of producing continuous behavior.
因此，选好解码器，并不意味着已经解决行为连续性问题。

77
00:07:22,451 --> 00:07:27,896
Prediction, queue management, and physical execution must agree about which timestamps remain editable.
预测、队列管理和物理执行，必须对哪些时间戳仍可修改达成一致。

78
00:07:27,911 --> 00:07:32,651
Our deployment chapter will make this commitment boundary explicit with a moving timeline.
部署章节会用一条移动时间轴，把这个不可随意修改的边界画清楚。

79
00:07:33,419 --> 00:07:40,419
For a practical comparison, freeze the observation pipeline and define one robot action contract first.
实际比较时，先固定观测流程，并定义一份机器人动作接口约定。

80
00:07:40,799 --> 00:07:46,159
Then vary the representation or decoder while keeping the data and evaluation budget comparable.
随后改变表示或解码器，同时尽量保持数据和评估预算可比。

81
00:07:46,619 --> 00:07:50,664
Measure both task completion and the delays that affect correction of the moved cup.
既测量任务完成情况，也测量影响杯子移动后纠正动作的各种延迟。

82
00:07:50,679 --> 00:07:57,239
Inspect failure trajectories, because a good average can hide jitter, ignored instructions, or late reactions.
还要检查失败轨迹，因为良好平均值可能掩盖抖动、忽略指令，或反应过晚。

83
00:07:57,819 --> 00:08:02,164
There is no reason to select the most complicated decoder before this evidence exists.
在获得这些证据之前，没有理由直接选择最复杂的解码器。

84
00:08:02,179 --> 00:08:08,179
Next, we use these distinctions to understand the major families of robot foundation policies.
下一章，我们用这些区分，理解机器人基础策略的主要路线。
